            <ArticleTitle>How accelerated atherosclerosis in SLE has changed our management of the disorder.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>228-31</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Basic science insights along with the assessment of risk factors so clearly documented by the Canadian and Hopkins cohorts in earlier papers of this special issue have clearly led to a change in the way rheumatologists manage SLE. This review will highlight specific ways it should alter our day to day treatment of lupus patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
